Here is a function in R to filter out words containing more than 5 letters:

```R
filter_words <- function(words) {
  filtered_words <- sapply(strsplit(words, " "), function(x) {
    if(nchar(x) > 5) {
      return(NULL)
    } else {
      return(x)
    }
  })
  return(unlist(filtered_words))
}

# Example usage
words <- c("apple", "banana", "cherry", "grape", "watermelon")
filtered_words <- filter_words(words)
print(filtered_words)
```

